terms=[('First cut in fourteen days, or you do not pay.','The first cut is the edited project film, complete enough to review: the story in order, with the interviews and the footage, before your revision round. The fourteen days start the day after the site day, or after the last coordinated interview if that comes later. The clock pauses only when we are waiting on a specific input that only you can give us, such as a signed release, and we name it when it happens. Our own editing and staffing never pause it. If the first cut is late, the project is free: anything you have paid is refunded in full and you keep every file.'),('Final delivery follows one round of notes.','You send one consolidated set of notes, gathered from everyone who needs a say. We make those changes and deliver the final film, the social cuts, the written case study, the page, the bid PDF and the stills. Final delivery has no fixed date because it depends on when your notes arrive; we confirm the date the day we receive them.'),('If the footage is not right, we come back on our dime.','If what we got does not hold up, we book another day and cover it. No change order, no mobilization fee.')]
