faqs=[('Why the founding rate?','We are building a commercial construction portfolio. The founding rate is for three qualifying projects, with written agreement on which approved work we can feature, and for exactly the scope listed here.'),('Who qualifies?','A commercial contractor or trade with a Central Ohio project where meaningful work is visible; a real use for the story, such as an upcoming bid, a prequalification or a sales follow-up; one authorized contact who can introduce the people involved; and approval to film the site and feature the approved work. The project-fit call is where we confirm it together.'),('What happens on the project-fit call?','You tell us about the job. We tell you straight whether it is a fit, recommend a story angle, and set out exactly what would be filmed, who would be interviewed and what you would get. You leave with that whether or not you go ahead.'),('Do we have to manage the shoot?','No. You introduce the people and name the authorized site contact. We handle the scheduling and the production. Your team still gives the agreed interviews, the permissions only it can give, and one round of approval.'),('Does one day cover the whole project?','The camera covers one agreed day on site: the work as it stands, the crew, the details. The story of the whole project comes from the interviews, with the people who ran it and the client it was built for. Filming more than one stage or location is a separate scope.'),('Does the client need to appear on camera?','An approved client interview makes the story stronger, so we confirm availability before reserving the project. If the client declines, we build a fact-led project story that does not imply a client endorsement.'),('Is fourteen days the final delivery date?','No. Fourteen days is the first cut: the edited project film, complete enough to review, before your revision round. The social cuts, the written case study, the page, the bid PDF and the stills follow with final delivery, after your one consolidated round of notes. We confirm that date when the notes arrive.'),('When does the fourteen day clock start, and what pauses it?','It starts the day after the completed site day, or after the last coordinated interview if that is later. It pauses only when we are waiting on a specific input that only you can give us, such as a signed release, and we name it when it happens. Our own editing and staffing never pause it.'),('What happens if the first cut is late?','The project is free. Anything you have already paid is refunded in full, and you keep every file we have made.'),('What is a consolidated revision round?','One set of notes, gathered from everyone who needs a say, sent to us in one place. We make those changes and deliver the final files.'),('What if the site is confidential?','This founding group needs permission to share approved work, so a project that has to stay private is not a fit for the founding rate. Ask us about a separate private scope.'),('Do we own the files?','You receive the final outputs and your organized raw footage. Licensed music and any other third-party material follow their license terms.'),('Will this guarantee a won bid?','No. We make evidence your team can use in proposals and sales conversations. Whether a buyer chooses you still depends on your offer, qualifications, price and competition.'),('Can we add another location or a crew film?','Yes, by separate scope and price, agreed before work starts. The founding package covers one project and one location.'),('What about ongoing work?','We talk about it after the first story, once we both know it is a good fit. The founding package stands on its own.'),('What if the weather turns?','We reschedule at no charge and the clock starts from the new date.')]
